## Root cause

**`runtime_soak_frontend`** — 1:1 race between writer cadence and freshness threshold. `codex_runtime_soak_and_production_equivalence_governor.py:233` enforces `age <= 900`, but the governor itself is the writer, fired by `ai-bot-codex-runtime-soak-production-equivalence-governor.timer` with `OnUnitActiveSec=15min` (900s). At each pass the prior self-written `operator_dashboard_payload.json` is ~900s old; subprocess startup + AccuracySec push it to 901+s and the strict `<= 900` flips it stale. Confirmed by `payloads.runtime_soak_frontend.age_seconds=901` in `codex_15m_status.json`.

**`replacement_readiness_scoreboard`** — fragile subprocess in `v2/backend/app/cli/v2_production_payload_freshness_refresher.py::_refresh_replacement_readiness_scoreboard()`. The other five `/latest/` descriptors the refresher owns are landing every 60s, so the loop is healthy. The scoreboard subprocess fires only intermittently (observed self-recovery from a 27-min drought at `05:12:47Z` mid-session). No explicit `cwd`, no `env={PYTHONPATH=…}`, no fallback restamp, and stderr log file is missing — silent failures, arbitrary drift.

